            <ArticleTitle>Onset during exercise of spontaneous coronary artery dissection and sudden death. Occurrence in a trained athlete: case report and review of prior cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>284-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report describes a spontaneous coronary artery dissection occurring during exercise in a long-distance runner who otherwise had a normal coronary arteriogram. This syndrome has been reported before and the two previous cases are reviewed. Coronary dissection is a rare cause of death during exercise.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
